        "narrative": "<p>The primary game fish in Gun Lake is lake trout.  The abundance was within the normal range for this lake class, and similar to the abundance in the only previous survey in 1974.  The average length of lake trout was 21.5\", and the largest sampled lake trout was 28.9\".  The lake trout in Gun Lake were relatively old and showed slow growth.  Other game fish present were smallmouth bass and yellow perch, but numbers were low.Tullibee and white sucker were also sampled.  Mean length of tullibee was 7.9\", and abundance was normal for this lake type.  White sucker numbers were low.</p>",
