        "narrative": "<p>Gun is a deep, clear, class 3 lake located south of Lac La Croix within the Boundary Waters Canoe Area.  Several species of fish were captured in 2008, however, lake trout are the primary focus of management.    <br> \n   <br> \nLake trout gill-net abundance was 0.67 fish/set, which was much lower than the previous investigation in 1996 (2.13 fish/set).  Net locations were adjusted in 2008 to target optimal thermal habitat for lake trout, therefore results may not be directly comparable to previous investigations.  Four year-classes were present and age ranged from 3-10 years.  Total length ranged from 10.9-28.5 inches and the mean was 19.6.  Mean weight was 3.18 pounds.   <br> \n <br> \nAngling was used to sample a total of 11 smallmouth bass during 5 hours of fishing (2 people fished for 2.5 hours each).  Smallmouth bass were also captured in deepwater gill nets, but below what is typically found in most class 3 lakes.  Total length ranged from 8.4 to 16.3 inches and age ranged from 3 to 9 years for both gear types combined.   <br> \n <br> \nTullibee gill-net abundance was 7.33 fish/set.  Total length ranged from 6.7-12.2 inches and the mean was 9.5.  Mean weight was 0.24 pounds.   <br> \n <br> \n</p>"
